{"availability":"available","full":"cekuu35/cekuu35","name":"cekuu35","description":"Cenk Kurtoglu — Next.js, TypeScript, Supabase RLS, public demos and evidence-backed digital products.","category":"Design","language":null,"stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-06-21T15:13:23Z","updated":"2026-09-01T09:02:59Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://cenkkurtoglu.com","topics":["freelance","nextjs","portfolio","react","rls","supabase","tailwindcss","typescript","website-template"],"demo":"https://apps.apple.com/tr/app/abonem-subscription-tracker/id6776748341","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:08.025Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:08.025Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:08.025Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T07:02:08.025Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["React","Next.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["I audit Supabase authorization boundaries. Most of my work is finding the cross-user and cross-tenant data leaks that a linter cannot see: a permissive policy silently cancelling a restrictive one, a membership join that is not isolated, or a service-role key reachable from a client path. The SQL is valid in all three cases, which is why they survive code review and pass tests.","If you arrived here from a Postgres or Supabase thread about RLS not working, anon key exposure, or SECURITY DEFINER bypassing your policies, start with the free tools below. The same SQL goes red on one branch and green on the other in about two seconds. No Docker, no Supabase account needed.","I also build and maintain Next.js, React and Node.js products; those are further down, labeled by evidence type so you can tell public source from live products, prototypes and private code."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cekuu35/cekuu35/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9a72d634ba0778aa8ff219571ef4b487079a981481a0b4e4e39c86bf6eabe318","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T07:02:08.110Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-